{"task_id": "Mbpp/11", "solution": "from dataclasses import dataclass\ndef remove_Occ(source: str, target: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Removes the first and last occurrences of a target character from a source string.\n    Returns the modified string or original if the target is not a single character or not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    target_char_obj = TargetCharacter(target)\n    if not target_char_obj.is_single_char():\n        return source # For an invalid target length, return the original source.\n\n    # Find all indices of the target character in the source string.\n    indices = [i for i, char in enumerate(source) if char == target]\n\n    if not indices:\n        return source # If target does not occur, return the original source.\n    elif len(indices) == 1:\n        # If target occurs only once, remove that single occurrence.\n        first_idx = indices[0]\n        result = source[:first_idx] + source[first_idx+1:]\n        return ResultString(result).value\n    else:\n        # If target occurs multiple times, remove the first and last occurrences.\n        first_idx = indices[0]\n        last_idx = indices[-1]\n        \n        # Construct the new string by concatenating parts around the removed indices.\n        result = source[:first_idx] + source[first_idx+1:last_idx] + source[last_idx+1:]\n        return ResultString(result).value"}
