{"task_id": "Mbpp/92", "solution": "class UndulatingChecker:\n    \"\"\"Encapsulates the algorithm to determine if a number is undulating.\"\"\"\n    def is_undulating(self, n: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Determines if the base-10 decimal digit sequence of integer n alternates.\"\"\"\n        return self._check_by_digits(abs(n))\n\n    def _check_by_digits(self, n_val: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Performs the O(d) single pass check for undulating property.\"\"\"\n        if n_val == 0:\n            return False  # Single digit 0 is not undulating (BR9)\n\n        temp_val_for_count = n_val\n        digit_count = 0\n        initial_divisor = 1\n\n        # Calculate digit_count and initial_divisor (10^(d-1)) in one O(d) pass.\n        if temp_val_for_count == 0:\n            digit_count = 1\n        else:\n            while temp_val_for_count > 0:\n                temp_val_for_count //= 10\n                digit_count += 1\n                if temp_val_for_count > 0:\n                    initial_divisor *= 10\n        \n        if digit_count < 2:\n            return False  # Numbers with less than two digits are not undulating (BR9)\n\n        # Extract first two digits using the calculated initial_divisor.\n        current_num = n_val\n        \n        A = (current_num // initial_divisor) % 10\n        current_num %= initial_divisor\n        initial_divisor //= 10\n\n        B = (current_num // initial_divisor) % 10\n        current_num %= initial_divisor\n        initial_divisor //= 10\n\n        if A == B:\n            return False  # Alternating digits must be distinct (BR1/BR2)\n\n        # Check remaining digits in a single O(d) pass.\n        for i in range(2, digit_count):\n            expected = A if i % 2 == 0 else B\n            \n            current_digit = (current_num // initial_divisor) % 10\n            \n            if current_digit != expected:\n                return False\n            \n            current_num %= initial_divisor\n            if initial_divisor > 1:\n                initial_divisor //= 10\n            \n        return True\ndef is_undulating(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an integer's base-10 decimal digits alternate between exactly two distinct digits.\n    Handles negative integers by considering their absolute value, and single-digit numbers are not undulating.\n    \"\"\"\n    checker = UndulatingChecker()\n    return checker.is_undulating(n)"}
