{"task_id": "Mbpp/95", "solution": "def Find_Min_Length(list_of_lists):\n    \"\"\"Compute the length of the shortest inner list in list_of_lists.\"\"\"\n    # Validate that the outer list is non-empty.\n    if not list_of_lists:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'list_of_lists' must not be empty.\")\n\n    min_length = float('inf') # Initialize with a value larger than any possible list length\n\n    # Iterate through inner lists, validating and computing minimum length.\n    for i, inner_list in enumerate(list_of_lists):\n        # Validate that each element of the outer list is itself a list.\n        if not isinstance(inner_list, list):\n            raise ValueError(f\"Element at index {i} is not a list (found type: {type(inner_list).__name__}).\")\n        min_length = min(min_length, len(inner_list))\n\n    return min_length"}
