{"task_id": "Mbpp/116", "solution": "def _concatenate(input_tuple) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Concatenates the decimal representations of tuple elements into a single integer.\n    Assumes input_tuple contains valid positive integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    return int(''.join(str(x) for x in input_tuple))\ndef tuple_to_int(input_tuple) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a tuple of positive integers into a single integer by concatenating\n    their decimal representations. Raises ValueError for invalid inputs.\n\n    :param input_tuple: A tuple of strictly positive integers.\n    :return: An integer formed by concatenating the tuple elements.\n    :raises ValueError: If input is not a tuple, or elements are not positive integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    _validate_input(input_tuple)\n    _validate_elements(input_tuple)\n    return _concatenate(input_tuple)"}
