{"task_id": "Mbpp/265", "solution": "from typing import Any, Iterable, List, Sequence\nclass ValidationError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"\n    Exception raised for invalid 'n' parameter.\n    Custom exception for validation errors.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str) -> None:\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n\n    def __str__(self) -> str:\n        return self.message\ndef validate_n(n: Any) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates that n is an integer greater than 0.\n    Raises ValidationError if n is invalid.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n <= 0:\n        raise ValidationError(\"n must be an integer > 0\")\n    return True\ndef list_split(input_list: Sequence[Any], n: int) -> List[List[Any]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Splits an input_list into n sublists, distributing elements by index modulo n.\n    Returns a new list containing exactly n sublists.\n    \"\"\"\n    validate_n(n)\n\n    result: List[List[Any]] = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n\n    for idx, val in enumerate(input_list):\n        result[idx % n].append(val)\n\n    return result"}
