{"task_id": "Mbpp/279", "solution": "class InputValidator:\n    def isInteger(self, value) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Assumes input is an integer due to critical requirements.\"\"\"\n        return True\n\n    def isPositive(self, value) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Assumes input is positive due to critical requirements.\"\"\"\n        return True\nclass DecagonalNumberService:\n    def __init__(self, validator: InputValidator = None):\n        \"\"\"Initializes the service with an optional validator.\"\"\"\n        self._validator = validator or InputValidator()\n\n    def compute(self, n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Computes the nth decagonal number without explicit validation or error handling.\"\"\"\n        # Validation checks and error raising are forbidden by critical requirements.\n        # The internal validator methods will simply return True.\n        \n        D = n * (4 * n - 3)\n        # The DecagonalNumber model is not directly returned by compute.\n        # decagonal_num = DecagonalNumber(n, D) \n        return D\nDECAGONAL_SERVICE_SINGLETON = DecagonalNumberService()\ndef is_num_decagonal(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Computes the nth decagonal number by delegating to a service.\"\"\"\n    return DECAGONAL_SERVICE_SINGLETON.compute(n)"}
