{"task_id": "Mbpp/429", "solution": "class InputTuple:\n    \"\"\"Encapsulates an input tuple of integers.\n    Provides methods for construction and direct access.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, elements: tuple[int, ...]) -> None:\n        self.elements = elements\n\n    def as_tuple(self) -> tuple[int, ...]:\n        \"\"\"Returns the encapsulated tuple of integers.\"\"\"\n        return self.elements\nclass ResultTuple:\n    \"\"\"Encapsulates a result tuple of integers.\n    Provides methods for construction and direct access.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, elements: tuple[int, ...]) -> None:\n        self.elements = elements\n\n    def as_tuple(self) -> tuple[int, ...]:\n        \"\"\"Returns the encapsulated tuple of integers.\"\"\"\n        return self.elements\nclass AndTuplesFunction:\n    \"\"\"A stateless domain service for computing elementwise bitwise AND.\"\"\"\n    def compute(self, a: InputTuple, b: InputTuple) -> ResultTuple:\n        \"\"\"Computes elementwise bitwise AND on the elements of two InputTuple objects.\n        Results are generated up to the length of the shorter input tuple.\n        \"\"\"\n        n = min(len(a.elements), len(b.elements))\n        results = [a.elements[i] & b.elements[i] for i in range(n)]\n        return ResultTuple(tuple(results))\ndef and_tuples(a: tuple[int, ...], b: tuple[int, ...]) -> tuple[int, ...]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the elementwise bitwise AND of two input tuples of integers.\n    The operation proceeds for elements up to the length of the shorter tuple.\n    \"\"\"\n    a_input = InputTuple(a)\n    b_input = InputTuple(b)\n    service = AndTuplesFunction()\n    result_obj = service.compute(a_input, b_input)\n    return result_obj.as_tuple()"}
