{"task_id": "Mbpp/563", "solution": "from typing import List, Tuple\ndef _find_quoted_values(input: str) -> List[Tuple[int, int, str]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Scans the input string for properly matched double-quote pairs.\n    Returns a list of (startIndex, endIndex, value) tuples in left-to-right order.\n    \"\"\"\n    found_values = []\n    in_quote = False\n    start_index = -1\n\n    for i, char in enumerate(input):\n        if char == '\"':\n            if not in_quote:\n                # Found opening quote\n                start_index = i\n                in_quote = True\n            else:\n                # Found closing quote\n                end_index = i\n                # Extract the inner content (excluding quotes)\n                value = input[start_index + 1:end_index]\n                found_values.append((start_index, end_index, value))\n                in_quote = False # Reset state after finding a matched pair\n                start_index = -1 # Reset start index\n    return found_values\ndef extract_values(input: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts the inner contents of double-quoted substrings from the input string.\n    Returns an ordered list of these values, or an empty list if none are found.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Use the internal helper to find all quoted value details\n    quoted_value_tuples = _find_quoted_values(input)\n\n    # Extract only the value string from each tuple, preserving order\n    return [item[2] for item in quoted_value_tuples]"}
