{"task_id": "Mbpp/724", "solution": "from .model import InputParameter, ComputationResult\nfrom .arithmetic import BigIntegerArithmetic\nfrom .digits import DigitSumCalculator\nclass BigIntegerArithmetic:\n    \"\"\"\n    Provides methods for arbitrary-precision integer arithmetic.\n    It computes base ** power using exact integer exponentiation.\n    \"\"\"\n    def pow(self, base: int, power: int) -> int:\n        return base ** power\nclass DigitSumCalculator:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the sum of decimal digits of the absolute value of an integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    def sumDigits(self, number: int) -> int:\n        return sum(int(digit) for digit in str(abs(number)))\ndef power_base_sum(base: int, power: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes base to the power, then sums the decimal digits of the absolute result.\n    This function uses exact integer arithmetic and returns an integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Input validation via IntegerValidator is omitted per critical requirements.\n\n    arithmetic_calculator = BigIntegerArithmetic()\n    result_value = arithmetic_calculator.pow(base, power)\n\n    digit_calculator = DigitSumCalculator()\n    digit_sum = digit_calculator.sumDigits(result_value)\n\n    return digit_sum"}
