{"task_id": "Mbpp/730", "solution": "def consecutive_duplicates(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Return a new list where each maximal run of consecutive elements equal by '==' is reduced to a single instance.\n    The input list remains unmodified, and an empty list is returned for an empty input.\"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return []\n\n    result = []\n    # Initialize a unique sentinel to indicate no previous element has been added yet.\n    last_added_element = object() \n\n    for element in input_list:\n        # If this is the first element or it's different from the last element added to result, append it.\n        if last_added_element is object() or element != last_added_element:\n            result.append(element)\n            last_added_element = element\n    \n    return result"}
