{"task_id": "Mbpp/751", "solution": "def check_min_heap(arr) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if the given array represents a min-heap.\n    Iterates through parent nodes, comparing each to its children.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return True\n\n    # The last potential parent node is at index floor((n - 2) / 2).\n    # We iterate from index 0 up to and including this last parent.\n    last_parent_idx = (n - 2) // 2\n\n    for i in range(last_parent_idx + 1):\n        left_child_idx = 2 * i + 1\n        # If the parent is greater than its left child, it's not a min-heap.\n        # Comparisons are allowed to raise TypeError for incomparable types, which propagates.\n        if arr[i] > arr[left_child_idx]:\n            return False\n\n        right_child_idx = 2 * i + 2\n        # Check if a right child exists before comparing.\n        if right_child_idx < n:\n            # If the parent is greater than its right child, it's not a min-heap.\n            if arr[i] > arr[right_child_idx]:\n                return False\n\n    return True"}
