{"task_id": "Mbpp/742", "solution": "import math\ndef _compute_surface_area(edge_length) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Computes the surface area using the formula. Assumes valid input.\"\"\"\n    return math.sqrt(3) * (edge_length ** 2)\ndef area_tetrahedron(edge_length):\n    \"\"\"\n    Compute total surface area of a regular tetrahedron.\n\n    Parameters:\n    - edge_length: numeric (int or float)\n\n    Returns:\n    - float: surface area = math.sqrt(3) * edge_length**2\n\n    Raises:\n    - TypeError if edge_length is not numeric\n    - ValueError if edge_length is negative\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(edge_length, (int, float)):\n        raise TypeError(\"edge_length must be a numeric type\")\n    if edge_length < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"edge_length must be non-negative\")\n\n    return _compute_surface_area(edge_length)"}
